{{Quote|Don't interrupt me when I'm monologuing.|Raxlo to [[Kai Brightstar]]|<ref name="Raxlo Strikes Back">{{YJA|Raxlo Strikes Back}}</ref>}}
'''Raxlo''' was a [[Gozzo]] who lived during the [[High Republic Era]] and was the head of the [[Raxlo Corporation]]. He often used his custom [[Raxlo's harvester|harvesting vehicle]] to deforest [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]]s in the name of maximizing profits.<ref name="Forest Defenders" /> Raxlo once disrupted the favorite meditation spot of the [[Poobian]] [[Jedi]] [[Jedi Initiate|Initiate]] [[Nubs]] by harvesting the inside of a [[Tenoo tree]] for its highly valuable sap.<ref name="Tree Troubles">{{YJA|Tree Troubles}}</ref>

Following several run-ins with the [[Tenoo]] Jedi younglings in which they thwarted his unsustainable business ventures, Raxlo turned to the [[water|snowy]] world [[Andraven]]. There, he attempted to [[mining|mine]] the valuable [[tenga rock]]s. He could effectively mine the energy-producing rocks with his harvester, but the heat generated by his [[laser]] was melting so much snow that it was compromising the incubation of [[wellagrin]] [[Wellagrin egg|eggs]]. Raxlo was stopped by Nubs and his friends [[Kai Brightstar]] and [[Lys Solay]], who saved the eggs. Raxlo, feeling dejected, confided in the young Jedi about his concerns of making a living if everything he does is somehow wrong. The Jedi and [[Andraven (species)|Andraven]] locals taught Raxlo that he could collaborate with community leaders to scout the most ecologically sustainable locations to mine the tenga rocks.<ref name="RSB">{{YJA|Raxlo Strikes Back}}</ref>

This conversation fundamentally changed Raxlo's business practices, turning him from a foe of the young Jedi into a friend. Raxlo worked with Andraven locals to maintain a steady customer base for tenga rocks while preserving the local environment. This work was so effective that the Andravens eventually began to see Raxlo as a hero, an identity the Gozzo struggled to fully accept until he worked with the young Jedi to stop the [[Ganguls]] from stealing his harvester and numerous tenga rocks.<ref name="Raxlo to the Rescue">{{YJA|Raxlo to the Rescue}}</ref>

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Raxlo first appeared in the [[2023]] second-half episode "[[Forest Defenders]]," voiced by [[Haley Joel Osment]].<ref name="Forest Defenders" />

